.\" Manpage for NekoWM
.\" Contact: yourname@example.com
.TH NEKOWM 1 "September 2025" "NekoWM 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nekowm \- a lightweight, stack-based tiling window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nekowm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISTACK_COUNT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NekoWM is a lightweight tiling window manager with split-based layouts. It manages windows in a stack-like fashion: each newly spawned window splits space with the previously added window in the current stack, recursively halving space as new windows appear.

NekoWM is designed as a single, self-contained binary with:
.IP \[bu] 2
No runtime dependencies beyond X11 libraries.
.IP \[bu] 2
No external configuration files or daemons.
.IP \[bu] 2
Static configuration at compile time via \fIsrc/headers/config.h\fR.

It only manages windows, providing essential window operations without runtime reconfiguration.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-split-toggle
Toggle split mode for the currently selected window.
.TP
.B \-\-exit-neko
Exit NekoWM.
.TP
.B \-\-close-focused
Close the currently focused window.
.TP
.B \-\-next-stack
Switch to the next stack.
.TP
.B \-\-previous-stack
Switch to the previous stack.
.TP
.B \-\-focus-next
Move focus to the next window in the stack.
.TP
.B \-\-focus-previous
Move focus to the previous window in the stack.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Fullscreen the currently selected window.
.TP
.B \-\-update-monitors
Update monitor mapping.
.TP
.B STACK_COUNT
Number of stacks to create (default: 10).

.SH KEYBINDINGS
Keybindings are defined in
.I src/headers/config.h
and applied at compile time. They cannot be changed at runtime.
.P
Example:
.IP
{ MOD1 | MOD2, XK_Return, "dmenu_run" }
.P
Default modifier keys:
.IP \[bu] 2
MOD1 = Alt
.IP \[bu] 2
MOD2 = Shift
.IP \[bu] 2
MOD3 = Control
.IP \[bu] 2
MOD4 = Super

.SH CONFIGURATION
NekoWM does not read configuration files at runtime. All customization is done by editing:
.I src/headers/config.h
and recompiling.

Available options:
.TS
allbox;
l l.
Option	Function
BAR_POSITION	Position of the bar (0 = Bottom, 1 = Top)
BAR_COLOR	Background color of the bar
BAR_TEXT_COLOR	Text color of the bar
BAR_HEIGHT	Height of the bar in pixels
BAR_BORDER	Width of the bar border
BAR_BORDER_COLOR	Color of the bar border
BORDER 	Border width of each mapped window
FOCUSED	Border color of the focused window
UNFOCUSED	Border color of unfocused windows
GAP	Gap between mapped windows
SOCKET	Enable or disable UNIX socket support
LOG	Enable or disable logging
BAR	Enable or disable bar rendering
SOCKET_PATH	Path for the UNIX socket
LOG_PATH	Path of the log file
.TE

.SH EXAMPLES
Run NekoWM with default settings:
.P
.B nekowm
.P
Run NekoWM with 5 stacks:
.P
.B nekowm 5
.P
Close the focused window:
.P
.B nekowm --close-focused

.SH FILES
NekoWM uses no runtime configuration files.

